OpenBSD VMs

obsd.sh installs, upgrades, and runs OpenBSD VMs under QEMU; guests use
a serial console and qcow2 disk images.

For design rationale and architecture specific details, see:
https://kirill.korins.ky/articles/openbsd-under-qemu/

Requirements

Install the required packages:

    pkg_add qemu libarchive u-boot-aarch64 u-boot-arm u-boot-octeon \
        u-boot-riscv64 opensbi talos-ii-pnor-bootkernel

The following patches are required for QEMU 11.1.1 and libslirp 4.9.4.
They are included in the OpenBSD -current QEMU port; OpenBSD 8.0
includes all except the hppa patch:

    sparc64:
      https://github.com/catap/openbios/commit/9151118aea489f9fffa40c60ee3b1d93383fb96b.patch
      https://github.com/catap/openbios/commit/8d5ed09f0420389a27394b7c1b7d40ae7aab9d32.patch
      https://github.com/catap/openbios/commit/cd90de7bda9006e2382d10302555a4cf825ea425.patch
      https://github.com/catap/openbios/commit/daa1b2595b2347e8031431dae1aeded976fd7057.patch

    powerpc64:
      https://patchew.org/QEMU/20260719145559.94342-1-kirill@korins.ky/

    QEMU/octeon:
      https://patchew.org/QEMU/20260719215455.96122-1-kirill@korins.ky/
      https://patchew.org/QEMU/20261029204609.38989-1-kirill@korins.ky/

    OpenBSD/macppc:
      https://patchew.org/QEMU/20261001230058.11465-1-kirill@korins.ky/
